                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5741538e-7023-3a57-a3de-5e745fa642a6",
                                        "entry_id": "f1def124-5fbf-3f0d-ac09-2bf441f2e0cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The long bone in the forearm, on the side of the thumb."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e544ba02-ca8f-4953-855b-e84e974abc24",
                                                "sense_id": "5741538e-7023-3a57-a3de-5e745fa642a6",
                                                "text": "It is also obvious, and proved by experiment, that the rotatory motions observed in the hand proceed from the rotatory motions of the radius."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "251b438a-0ce9-3a90-a476-720bde0d38cd",
                                        "entry_id": "f1def124-5fbf-3f0d-ac09-2bf441f2e0cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The lighter bone (or fused portion of bone) in the forelimb of an animal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e20037b-1a4c-335c-a826-a9833a4a6477",
                                        "entry_id": "f1def124-5fbf-3f0d-ac09-2bf441f2e0cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One of the major veins of the insect wing, between the subcosta and the media; the vein running along the costal edge of the discal cell."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0cb249c3-4764-3fcf-896f-809af418acf9",
                                        "entry_id": "f1def124-5fbf-3f0d-ac09-2bf441f2e0cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A line segment between any point of a circle or sphere and its center."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "405d6389-0c2d-41e6-96cf-a42547ca4649",
                                                "sense_id": "0cb249c3-4764-3fcf-896f-809af418acf9",
                                                "text": "Fatima claims to have visited all the bars within a five-mile radius of her Manhattan apartment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2371c5ea-0a5b-454c-8d34-f5d337ec1982",
                                                "sense_id": "0cb249c3-4764-3fcf-896f-809af418acf9",
                                                "text": "We start with spherical geometries. The two geometries on spheres of radiuses R₁ and R₂ are obviously identical if R₁ = R₂; moreover, the converse also holds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3707de8-e0d8-4ec2-986c-ad3e9d69dc0d",
                                                "sense_id": "0cb249c3-4764-3fcf-896f-809af418acf9",
                                                "text": "The velocity dispersions of early- and late-type galaxies in compact groups change little with groupcentric radius; the radii sampled are less than 100~h#123;-1#125; kpc, smaller than the radii typically sampled by members of massive clusters of galaxies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "01ffa226-a43a-3fb3-a42c-ea90c9c64b86",
                                        "entry_id": "f1def124-5fbf-3f0d-ac09-2bf441f2e0cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The length of this line segment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74af8f5f-5c0f-487d-a951-b92e1c6df2d4",
                                                "sense_id": "01ffa226-a43a-3fb3-a42c-ea90c9c64b86",
                                                "text": "This contribution reduces with increasing distance p from the emitting surface element dA, due to conservation of energy, as the wave energy distributed across the spherical wave front remains constant, while the radius increases during ..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37f33502-1b80-3040-9d9d-2b5aa404387d",
                                        "entry_id": "f1def124-5fbf-3f0d-ac09-2bf441f2e0cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything resembling a radius, such as the spoke of a wheel, the movable arm of a sextant, or one of the radiating lines of a spider's web."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2b4d48b-7daa-4499-9f2e-9b710ae3e974",
                                                "sense_id": "37f33502-1b80-3040-9d9d-2b5aa404387d",
                                                "text": "[…] I can do more with a Quadrant, Sextant or Octant, of 1 foot Radius, furniſhed with Teleſcopical Sights and Screws, then ^([sic]) can poſſibly be done with any other Inſtrument, furniſhed only with Common Sights, though 10, 20, 30, nay threeſcore foot Radius; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "44be13b1-4c1c-3ff0-90ee-8509a47a9dc0",
                                        "entry_id": "f1def124-5fbf-3f0d-ac09-2bf441f2e0cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The minimum eccentricity of any vertex, for a given graph."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "radius",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de9861de-e494-32a3-ab64-dfc2a4d71972",
                                        "entry_id": "97794ed5-17ce-33bd-ad88-479cf133bb34",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To give a rounded edge to."
                                        ],
